**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The two pure halves of copying experiments between kits: how a copied experiment is named, and which library versions it needs (001 §H 'Between kits: Copy experiments from another kit… brings the experiments with their setups, data files and the items they use'; .spec-md §3.15; the S6 brief: each experiment is copied with the library snapshots it needs, and clashing names get S4.1's suffix rule). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `Experiment` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) gains `static member renumberedFor (taken : ExperimentId list) (incoming : Experiment list) : Experiment list`. An experiment is stored under its id (`E<n>`, `ExperimentId.fileStem`, step 146), so a name clash is an id clash, and the suffix rule of an id-named file is the next free id. In order, an incoming experiment keeps its id when no id of `taken` and no id given to an earlier incoming experiment equals it; otherwise it takes the `next` (`Experiments.fs:139`) of the highest id among `taken`, every incoming id and every id given so far. Only `id` changes, and the order is kept. S8.3 and S9.1, which give experiments template names, carry the rule over to names. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`: the depth-first walk of `KitLibraryContext.snapshotReferences` (step 139) moves into `referenceClosure (resolve : EntryReference -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, KitLibraryError>) (references : EntryReference list) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope list, KitLibraryError>`, declared before `KitLibraryContext`'s members: it resolves each reference through `resolve`, then walks each resolved envelope's `content.references` (step 137) depth first and in order, visiting every version (`libraryVersionRef`, step 137) once, and answers the visited envelopes in visit order; the first error stops it. `snapshotReferences` calls it with its own resolution (the kit's snapshot of a version, otherwise the library's held or latest envelope) and then pins and writes the versions the kit lacks exactly as before, so its walk exists once. No other member is added. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `copied experiments keep their ids unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free id`: with `taken` [1; 2], incoming E2 and E3 answer E4 (E2's experiment) and E3, in that order; with `taken` empty the incoming are unchanged; with `taken` [5], incoming E1, E5 and E2 answer E1, E6 and E2; every field but `id` is unchanged. `KitLibraryTests` (step 139) gains `the closure of references walks each entry's references depth first, each version once`: over a resolver reading `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`'s envelopes (`EntryVersionReference` by id and version, `EntryLatestReference` by the highest version, anything else `UnheldEntryErr`), the references [multilayer v1; multilayer v1] (`SampleIds.multilayerQwId`) answer the sample, then each of its materials followed by that material's category, each version once, in the order step 139's first fact writes them; a reference to a test-local GUID answers `UnheldEntryErr`. Every other `KitLibraryTests` fact passes as written.

**Acceptance.** After the copy's pure halves land, `Experiment.renumberedFor` MUST keep every free id and give a clashing experiment the next free id, and `KitLibrary.referenceClosure` MUST hold the one depth-first walk that `snapshotReferences` calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `copied experiments keep their ids unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free id` and `the closure of references walks each entry's references depth first, each version once`, the count rising by 2, with every other `KitLibraryTests` fact passing as written; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
